-- KEY INSIGHTS
-- ============================================================

--
-- 1. TOP HAPPIEST COUNTRIES
--    Finland, Denmark, Switzerland, and Iceland lead the 2021 rankings.
--    All four share high social support (≥ 1.526), strong life expectancy
--    scores, and relatively low corruption perception — suggesting these
--    factors act together rather than independently.
--
-- 2. EUROPE DOMINATES
--    European countries hold the top five positions. Their combination of
--    high GDP per capita, robust social support systems, and low corruption
--    appears to be the defining cluster of characteristics. North America
--    (US at rank 19) scores well on GDP but lower on freedom and social
--    support relative to Nordic peers.
--
-- 3. DRIVERS OF HAPPINESS
--    GDP per capita and social support show the strongest apparent
--    relationship with happiness score in this dataset. Freedom to make
--    life choices also correlates positively. Generosity and perceptions
--    of corruption show weaker direct correlations at this sample size,
--    though they likely matter more in a full global dataset.

